.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt DOT_CLEAN 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dot_clean
.Nd merge AppleDouble files back into their files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl fmnsv
.Op Fl -keep Ns = Ns Cm mostrecent | dotbar | native
.Ar dir ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Volumes that cannot keep extended attributes, resource forks or Finder
information store them for
.Ar name
in a separate AppleDouble file,
.Pa ._ Ns Ar name .
.Nm
walks each
.Ar dir ,
puts what each such file holds back on the file it belongs to, and
removes it.
When both have an attribute,
.Fl -keep
says which one stays:
.Bl -tag -width mostrecent
.It Cm mostrecent
the newer of the two files (the default)
.It Cm dotbar
the AppleDouble file's
.It Cm native
the file's own
.El
.Pp
The other options:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f
Only the files directly in
.Ar dir ,
not those below.
.It Fl m
Remove the AppleDouble files even when merging failed.
.It Fl n
Remove AppleDouble files whose file does not exist.
.It Fl s
Follow symbolic links.
.It Fl v
Say what is merged.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xattr 1 ,
.Xr copyfile 3
.Sh HISTORY
Minkar's
.Nm
is its own.
